        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12317527/comment/12331151",
          "id": "12331151",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=fmeschbe",
            "name": "fmeschbe",
            "key": "fmeschbe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Felix Meschberger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Shouldn't the QNameResolver interface be placed in the name package just like the QName class itself ?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=fmeschbe",
            "name": "fmeschbe",
            "key": "fmeschbe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Felix Meschberger",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2005-10-03T19:31:51.000+0000",
          "updated": "2005-10-03T19:31:51.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12317527/comment/12331171",
          "id": "12331171",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Sounds great! +1 from me, especially the LRUMap is a nice touch, no need to worry about DoS threats due to this.\n\nDesign comment: The NamespaceRegistryImpl dependency seems out of place. How about the following structure?\n\norg.apache.jackrabbit.name:\n    public interface NamespaceListener\n    public interface QNameResolver\n    public class StandardQNameResolver implements QNameResolver\n    public class CachingQNameResolver implements QNameResolver, NamespaceListener\n\nThe static QName.toJCRName and QName.fromJCRName methods could be moved to StandardQNameResolver to simplify the QName class.\nThe CachingQNameResolver could  be implemented as a decorator on top of another QNameResolver implementation (StandardQNameResolver by default).\nClient code should register and deregister the CachingQNameResolver as a namespace change listener.\n\nThis structure would add a tiny amount of overhead (a virtual vs. a static method call + some extra object instances), but would IMHO add much flexibility to the resolution process while keeping the package boundaries nice and solid.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2005-10-03T23:49:17.000+0000",
          "updated": "2005-10-03T23:49:17.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12317527/comment/12331487",
          "id": "12331487",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=mreutegg",
            "name": "mreutegg",
            "key": "mreutegg",
            "avatarUrls": {
